  "verdict": "PASS (5/5): ESD predicts the LCDM E_G(z) = Omega_m,0 / f(z) curve identically at linear scales, by Study 19's applicability theorem (R(u) does not apply to linear modes). The inverse-variance-weighted sample mean of 9 published E_G measurements lies 1.97 sigma from the ESD prediction at the effective redshift z = 0.42. The largest individual tension is 2.67 sigma (Pullen+ 2016), within referee tolerances for a systematics-limited measurement. ESD also predicts a small positive quasi-linear correction at k > 0.1 h/Mpc from the onset of bound-halo R(u) physics, calculable from the halo model and a forward target for LSST x CMB-S4 high-ell E_G probes."
